== ERRATUM (appended, not silent) ==
The table above printed "theory n(n+1)/2" with values 1, 3, 6, ... — that column
was a leftover from the first (wrong) tail prior, corrected in the docstring
BEFORE the run but not in this print statement. The intended theory column is
n^2/(2*pi) = 0.159*n^2. The fit itself never used any theory value: k_n is
data-fit from consecutive cutoff pairs, so every extrapolated lambda_n above is
unaffected. Empirical finding: k_n = 0.1196*n^2 (2% stable across cutoff
pairs), 25% below the crude asymptotic n^2/(2*pi) — the low-gamma corrections
(theta = 2*arctan(1/(2*gamma)) < 1/gamma) and the N(T) constant terms all push
the effective constant down. Script print line fixed post-hoc; .out preserved.
